Remove Duplicates from Sorted List II (LeetCode 82)

Optimal Solution

Approach:
Since the linked list is sorted, duplicate values always come together.
Traverse the list using temp.
Keep a pointer prev to store the last node that is confirmed unique.
For every node:
Check if the next node has the same value.
If duplicates are found:
Store the duplicate value.
Skip all nodes having that value using nextNode.
Delete the first node of the duplicate sequence also.
Connect prev with the next unique node.
If duplicates start from the head, update head.
If no duplicate is found:
Move prev and temp forward.

Idea: If a value appears more than once, remove all nodes having that value.

Time Complexity: O(n)
Every node is visited only once.

Space Complexity: O(1)
No extra data structure is used.

Code :

/**
 * Definition for singly-linked list.
 * struct ListNode {
 *     int val;
 *     ListNode *next;
 *     ListNode() : val(0), next(nullptr) {}
 *     ListNode(int x) : val(x), next(nullptr) {}
 *     ListNode(int x, ListNode *next) : val(x), next(next) {}
 * };
 */

class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* deleteDuplicates(ListNode* head) {

        ListNode* temp = head;
        ListNode* prev = nullptr;

        while (temp != nullptr) {

            ListNode* nextNode = temp->next;

            // Duplicate sequence found
            if (nextNode != nullptr && temp->val == nextNode->val) {

                int duplValue = temp->val;

                // Skip all duplicate nodes
                while (nextNode != nullptr && nextNode->val == duplValue) {

                    ListNode* dupl = nextNode;
                    nextNode = nextNode->next;

                    delete dupl;
                }

                // Delete the first node of duplicate sequence
                delete temp;


                // If duplicate sequence starts from head
                if (prev == nullptr) {
                    head = nextNode;
                }
                else {
                    prev->next = nextNode;
                }

                // Move to next unique node
                temp = nextNode;
            }

            else {

                // Current node is unique
                prev = temp;
                temp = temp->next;
            }
        }

        return head;
    }
};

